<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Sample Webpage</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 20px;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            color: #333;
        }
        header {
            background: #35424a;
            color: #ffffff;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .container {
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-top: 15px;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .btn {
            display: inline-block;
            background: #e8491d;
            color: #ffffff;
            padding: 10px 15px;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .btn:hover {
            background: #333333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
        <p>A simple sample page structured with HTML5</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>About This Page</h2>
        <p>This is a foundational HTML document. It contains a header, a main content container, text formatting, and structural styling via internal CSS.</p>
        
        <h3>Key Features Included:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Responsive Viewport:</strong> Optimized for mobile and desktop screens.</li>
            <li><strong>Semantic Tags:</strong> Uses standard structural elements like <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Styled Elements:</strong> Clean typography and custom button design.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Want to learn more about web development? Visit the official documentation.</p>
        <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/html/" target="_blank" class="btn">Learn HTML Basics</a>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
